{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["And since they are all sacrifices of lesser sanctity, impurity is forbidden both in those who eat and in that which is eaten, and the liability of excision falls upon an impure person who ate that which was pure — ״who draws near to eat of the pure sacrifice while his impurity is upon him״ — for he profanes the sacred."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The lemma quoted in Hebrew appears to be a paraphrase of Leviticus 7:20 rather than the verse under comment (7:19); retained as Sforno gives it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:53.418298406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}